Compliance with constitutional rights (e.g., Fourth Amendment) and data protection laws (e.g., GDPR) is mandatory. Mass or unauthorized surveillance violates fundamental rights and is prohibited. Government agencies must demonstrate necessity, proportionality, and legality—ensuring that privacy protections are not circumvented under the guise of security.

